    "category": "Recursion",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "An encoded string follows the rule: Letters are appended directly. A digit d means the entire current decoded string is repeated d times. Given an encoded string s and an integer K, return the K-th character in the decoded string without explicitly constructing the decoded string. Solve the problem recursively.",
